[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]
[**
Module contains queries with ecore::EObject as receiver,
used as an entry point for accessing global configuration
values that are not tied to any specific UML element.
Includes queries for RDF URI mapping tokens
(uml-map-rdf property) and test package names.
/]
[module eobjectQuery(
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[import ucmism2t::services::PropertiesService /]

[**
Returns a sequence of RDF mapping token strings from the
property "uml-map-rdf", split by comma.

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
/]
[query public u_mappedUcmisItemsRdfTokens(
    anEObject : ecore::EObject) : Sequence(String) =
  'uml-map-rdf'.getPropertyValue()
    .replaceAll('\\s+', '')
    .tokenize(',')
/]

[**
Returns a sequence of source IRI strings from the RDF mapping
tokens (the part before ">").

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
/]
[query public u_mappedUcmisItemsRdf(
    anEObject : ecore::EObject) : Sequence(String) =
  anEObject.u_mappedUcmisItemsRdfTokens()
    ->select(s1 | s1.contains('>'))
    ->collect(s2 | s2.tokenize('>')->at(1))
/]

[**
Returns a sequence of target IRI strings from the RDF mapping
tokens (the part after ">").

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
/]
[query public u_mappedUcmisItemsRdfTargets(
    anEObject : ecore::EObject) : Sequence(String) =
  anEObject.u_mappedUcmisItemsRdfTokens()
    ->select(s1 | s1.contains('>'))
    ->collect(s2 | s2.tokenize('>')->at(2))
/]

[**
Returns a sequence of type names from the "uml-union-types"
property, split by comma. Each named type is understood to have
its own dedicated string-or-object union handling in the target
formats (e.g. Identifier), configured explicitly rather than
detected structurally, since nothing in a UML DataType's own
attributes signals that it should also accept a bare scalar value.

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
/]
[query public u_unionTypeNames(
    anEObject : ecore::EObject) : Sequence(String) =
  'uml-union-types'.getPropertyValue()
    .replaceAll('\\s+', '')
    .tokenize(',')
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of package names defined in the property TEST_PACKAGE.

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
/]
[query public u_testPackages(anEObject : ecore::EObject) : OrderedSet(String) =
  'TEST_PACKAGE'.getPropertyValue()
    .substituteAll(' ', '')
    .tokenize(',')
    ->asOrderedSet()
/]

[**
Returns the standard RDF/OWL/UCMIS namespace pairs from the
"rdf-static-namespaces" property, as "prefix>namespace" tokens —
NOT split into Sequence{prefix, namespace} pairs, because Acceleo's
collect auto-flattens whenever a lambda returns a collection per
iteration, which silently corrupts a Sequence(Sequence(String))
built this way. Each token is tokenized by '>' only at the point of
use (see ttl_prefixes, validateNamespaceConflicts,
u_combinedNamespaces), using the same "key > value" delimited-list
syntax as uml-map-rdf. Example property value:

  rdf-static-namespaces = \
    rdf   > http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#  , \
    rdfs  > http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#        , \
    owl   > http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#               , \
    xsd   > http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#            , \
    dc    > http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/             , \
    skos  > http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#         , \
    ucmis > http://ddialliance.org/Specification/UCMIS/1.0/RDF/

Adding, removing, or changing a static namespace is a configuration
change only — no template or query needs to change as a result.

@param anEObject - Only used as entry point.
@return A sequence of "prefix>namespace" tokens.
/]
[query public u_staticNamespaces(anEObject : ecore::EObject) : Sequence(String) =
  'rdf-static-namespaces'.getPropertyValue()
    .replaceAll('\\s+', '')
    .tokenize(',')
    ->select(token | token.contains('>'))
/]
